<section class="hero"><div class="hero-t">
<p class="kick">Wash &middot; Wear &middot; Keep</p>
<h1>Clothes do not wear out. They get washed out.</h1>
<p class="lead">Attirex is an independent clothing-care site. Read any care label, get a mark out before it sets, and load the machine so your wardrobe survives it.</p>
<p class="hero-cta"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Use the three tools</a> <a class="btn gh" href="laundry-guide.html">Laundry guide</a></p></div>
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1729487151777-b4be9098ecbb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=75" alt="A rack of shirts and trousers in a store" width="1000" height="700" fetchpriority="high"></section>
<div class="claims"><div class="wrap"><span>10 care symbols decoded</span><span>8 stains, step by step</span><span>No sponsored brands</span><span>Free, no sign-up</span></div></div>
<section><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-h"><p class="kick">Where it goes wrong</p><h2>Three habits that quietly ruin clothes</h2><p>None of them feel like damage at the time, which is exactly why they keep happening.</p></div>
<div class="alt"><div class="alt-t"><span class="n">01</span><h3>Washing too hot, too often</h3><p>Heat is what kills elastic, shrinks cotton and lifts dye. Most clothes are washed twice as often and twice as hot as they need, and the machine is where a wardrobe actually wears out.</p></div>
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1611090925566-b1fc31065f63?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=75" alt="A white and blue clothes iron" width="700" height="525" loading="lazy"></div>
<div class="alt"><div class="alt-t"><span class="n">02</span><h3>Leaving a mark to deal with later</h3><p>Almost every stain comes out if it is treated the same day and almost none come out after a hot tumble dry. The difference between a saved shirt and a ruined one is usually twenty minutes.</p></div>
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1776617587745-0d0fac260555?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=75" alt="Close-up of textured grey fabric with stitching" width="700" height="525" loading="lazy"></div>
<div class="alt"><div class="alt-t"><span class="n">03</span><h3>Cramming the drum</h3><p>A packed machine cannot rinse. Detergent stays in the cloth, the smell comes back on the second wear, and everything comes out creased enough to need pressing it did not need.</p></div>
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633680889715-2c9752bf0840?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=75" alt="A close view of an iron on blue cloth" width="700" height="525" loading="lazy"></div>
</div></section>
<section class="tools" id="tools"><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-h"><p class="kick">Free tools</p><h2>Answer it before the machine starts</h2><p>Everything runs in your browser. Nothing is saved and nothing is sent anywhere.</p></div>
<div class="tool" id="symbols"><h3>Care Symbol Reader</h3><p>Pick the symbol you are squinting at and find out what it is asking for.</p>
<div class="tool-grid"><div><div class="fld"><label for="sym">Symbol on the label</label><select id="sym"><option value="normal">Tub, no bar &mdash; normal wash</option><option value="gentle">Tub with one bar &mdash; gentle</option><option value="hand">Hand in a tub &mdash; hand wash</option><option value="nowash">Crossed tub &mdash; do not wash</option><option value="tumble">Circle in a square &mdash; tumble dry</option><option value="notumble">Crossed square &mdash; no tumble</option><option value="iron2">Iron with two dots</option><option value="noiron">Crossed iron</option><option value="bleach">Crossed triangle &mdash; no bleach</option><option value="dryclean">Circle &mdash; dry clean</option></select></div>
<figure style="margin:0"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1619792423784-6c298b30299a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=75" alt="Purple fabric with a white button" width="700" height="525" loading="lazy" style="aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:cover"></figure></div>
<div class="out" id="symOut"></div></div></div>
<div class="tool" id="stains"><h3>Stain Guide</h3><p>What to reach for, in what order, and what will set the mark for good.</p>
<div class="tool-grid"><div><div class="fld"><label for="stain">What is on it?</label><select id="stain"><option value="grease">Grease or oil</option><option value="coffee">Coffee or tea</option><option value="redwine">Dark fruit or berry juice</option><option value="ink">Ink</option><option value="sweat">Perspiration marks</option><option value="mud">Mud</option><option value="makeup">Make-up</option><option value="sun">Fading from sunlight</option></select></div>
<p style="font-size:.92rem;color:#5A635F;margin:0">Work from the back of the fabric where you can, and keep heat away until the mark has gone completely.</p></div>
<div class="out" id="stOut"></div></div></div>
<div class="tool" id="load"><h3>Wash Load Planner</h3><p>Drum fill, temperature, spin speed and how much detergent a load of this size actually needs.</p>
<div class="tool-grid"><div><div class="fgrid"><div class="fld"><label for="ldKg">Dry weight (kg)</label><input id="ldKg" type="number" min="0.5" max="15" step="0.5" value="4"></div>
<div class="fld"><label for="ldDrum">Machine drum</label><select id="ldDrum"><option value="small">Small (5 kg)</option><option value="mid" selected>Medium (7 kg)</option><option value="large">Large (9 kg)</option><option value="xl">Extra large (11 kg)</option></select></div></div>
<div class="fgrid"><div class="fld"><label for="ldType">Load type</label><select id="ldType"><option value="everyday">Everyday clothes</option><option value="towels">Towels</option><option value="bedding">Bedding</option><option value="delicates">Delicates</option><option value="sports">Sportswear</option></select></div>
<div class="fld"><label for="ldSoil">How dirty?</label><select id="ldSoil"><option value="light">Lightly worn</option><option value="normal" selected>Normal</option><option value="heavy">Heavily soiled</option></select></div></div></div>
<div class="out" id="ldOut"></div></div></div>
</div></section>
<section><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-h"><p class="kick">Long reads</p><h2>Two guides, start to finish</h2></div>
<div class="rows">
<article class="grow"><div class="gn">01</div>
<div><h3>The Laundry Guide</h3><p>Sorting, temperature, detergent, drying and pressing, plus the machine maintenance nobody mentions until something smells. Written for one ordinary washing machine.</p><p style="margin:0"><a class="btn gh" href="laundry-guide.html">Read the guide</a></p></div>
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1669207261606-24c6a523cd0e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=760&q=75" alt="A rack of clothes" width="760" height="428" loading="lazy"></article>
<article class="grow"><div class="gn">02</div>
<div><h3>The Wardrobe Guide</h3><p>Storage, moths, hangers, seasonal rotation and repair: what to do with clothes during the long periods when you are not wearing them, which is most of their life.</p><p style="margin:0"><a class="btn gh" href="wardrobe-guide.html">Read the guide</a></p></div>
<img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1722942114764-fb0f27086089?auto=format&fit=crop&w=760&q=75" alt="A white wardrobe with clothes hanging on a rail" width="760" height="428" loading="lazy"></article>
</div></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-h"><p class="kick">Questions</p><h2>Asked over and over</h2></div>
<div class="faq2"><div><h3>What do the symbols on a care label actually mean?</h3><p>There are five families: a tub for washing, a triangle for bleaching, a square for drying, an iron for pressing and a circle for professional cleaning. Dots mean temperature, bars under a symbol mean a gentler cycle, and a cross means do not do it at all.</p></div><div><h3>Is 30&deg;C really enough to get clothes clean?</h3><p>For everyday clothes, yes. Modern detergents are built to work cold, and the agitation does most of the cleaning. Save 60&deg;C for towels, bedding and anything that has been near illness, where you want the heat for hygiene rather than for dirt.</p></div><div><h3>Why do my clothes still smell after washing?</h3><p>Usually an overloaded drum, too much detergent, or a machine that needs cleaning. Clothes need room to move; excess detergent leaves residue that holds odour; and the seal and drawer of a washing machine grow a film that smells. Run an empty hot cycle monthly.</p></div><div><h3>Should I use fabric conditioner?</h3><p>Rarely. It coats fibres, which reduces absorbency in towels and traps odour in sportswear. On cotton shirts it does little that a good shake and a careful hang will not. If you like the softness, use half what the bottle suggests.</p></div><div><h3>How do I stop dark clothes fading?</h3><p>Wash them inside out, at 30&deg;C, with a detergent for colours, and dry them out of direct sun. Most fading is caused by heat, friction and light rather than by water, so a shorter, cooler cycle and line drying in shade buys years.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="nl"><div class="wrap"><div><p class="kick">Newsletter</p><h2>The Attirex Fold</h2>
<p>One short email a month: a stain solved, a label decoded, and whatever we have added to the guides. No spam, unsubscribe any time.</p></div>
<div><p><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@attirex.com?subject=The%20Attirex%20Fold&body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></p><p style="font-size:.92rem;margin:0">Your email app opens with the sign-up ready to send, so nothing is stored here until you send it.</p></div></div></section>
